' Prices of production: class model
' Companion notes: notes/prices-of-production.md — full stereotype legend: notes/stereotypes.md
'
' Competition among many capitals forces a general rate of profit and
' prices of production. That only redistributes surplus value already
' produced. Commercial capital takes the same average; shop labour
' creates no s (Marx, Capital III, Part 2; SPGB).

@startuml prices-of-production
title VII. Prices of production — surplus value redistributed, not replaced
caption Competition levels the rate of profit; it does not create s: notes/prices-of-production.md

hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<abstract det.>> #E3F2FD
  BackgroundColor<<social relation>> #EDE7F6
  BackgroundColor<<historically specific>> #FFEBEE
}

package "I. Surplus value is still produced in production" as P1 {
  class SurplusValue <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    unpaid labour
    social pool : Σs
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class IndustrialCapital <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    capital in production
    c + v advanced
    produces s
  }
}

package "II. Why sale at value cannot last" as P2 {
  class OrganicComposition <<social relation>> <<historically specific>> {
    c / v
    differs by branch
  }
  class CostPrice <<historically specific>> {
    c + v used up
    not yet profit
  }
  class SaleAtValue <<abstract det.>> {
    {abstract}
    limiting case: commodities
    exchange at their values
    rates of profit stay unequal
  }
}

package "III. Competition forms a general rate" as P3 {
  class CapitalistCompetition <<social relation>> <<historically specific>> {
    many capitals
    (full definition: accumulation.puml)
  }
  class CapitalFlow <<historically specific>> {
    capital moves toward
    the higher rate of profit
  }
  class GeneralRateOfProfit <<social relation>> <<historically specific>> {
    tendency : Σs / Σ(c + v)
    not a political average
  }
  class AverageProfit <<historically specific>> {
    general rate × capital advanced
    Σ average profit = Σs
  }
  class PriceOfProduction <<historically specific>> {
    cost-price + average profit
    the form value takes
    under competition of many capitals
  }
}

package "IV. The same average, including commerce" as P4 {
  class CommercialCapital <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    capital in buying and selling
    produces no s
  }
  class CommercialProfit <<historically specific>> {
    share of s
    not a second source
  }
  class IndustrialProfit <<historically specific>> {
    share of s remaining
    with functioning industrial capital
    (also in finance.puml)
  }
}

IndustrialCapital *-- SurplusValue : appropriates
IndustrialCapital --> OrganicComposition : has
IndustrialCapital --> CostPrice : advances
SaleAtValue --> OrganicComposition : would leave rates\nunequal given
CapitalistCompetition --> CapitalFlow : compels
CapitalFlow --> SaleAtValue : rules out as\na lasting state
CapitalFlow --> GeneralRateOfProfit : forms
SurplusValue --> GeneralRateOfProfit : social pool Σs
GeneralRateOfProfit --> AverageProfit : determines
CostPrice --> PriceOfProduction : plus average profit
AverageProfit --> PriceOfProduction : enters
AverageProfit --> SurplusValue : exhausts the pool\n(does not enlarge)
IndustrialCapital --> AverageProfit : tends to receive
CommercialCapital --> AverageProfit : tends to receive
IndustrialCapital --> IndustrialProfit : receives as
CommercialCapital --> CommercialProfit : receives as
IndustrialProfit --|> AverageProfit
CommercialProfit --|> AverageProfit
IndustrialCapital --> CommercialCapital : sells below\nfinal price so both
CapitalistCompetition ..> CommercialCapital : same coercive law

P1 -[hidden]right-> P2
P2 -[hidden]right-> P3
P3 -[hidden]down-> P4

note as NPool
  **One pool, many rates become one rate**
  High c/v branches capture more profit
  than they produce in s; low c/v
  branches capture less. The deviations
  cancel. Total profit = total surplus
  value. Labour remains the source.
end note

note bottom of SaleAtValue
  Useful only as a baseline (Capital III,
  ch. 8–9): isolate what competition
  adds. Under real mobility of capital
  it cannot persist.
end note

note right of CommercialCapital
  If retailing paid more than
  manufacturing, capital would leave
  the factory for the shop until the
  rates came into line. Shop labour
  still creates no s.
end note

@enduml
